<title>UK: UK reserves fall underlying $98 mln in August.</title>
<headline>UK reserves fall underlying $98 mln in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's gold and currency reserves fell an underlying $98 million in August, the Treasury said. (IN MLN DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>					 AUGUST		 JULY</p>
<p> Underlying reserves	     -98		     -17</p>
<p>NOTE - Market forecast $25 million fall in underlying reserves.  </p>
<p>The underlying change excludes factors included in the total change (IN MLN OF DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)-</p>
<p>				   AUGUST		   JULY</p>
<p> Actual reserves		-113		   +2,656</p>
<p> Total actual reserves     47.95 billion	 48.07 billion</p>
<p> Repayments under the</p>
<p> exchange cover scheme (ECS)  -15		    -4</p>
<p>--London newsroom - +44 171 542 6701</p>
